  "uniqueRetainedOwnNote": "The Kaplan-Meier event-fraction calculation does not specify a constant between-group hazard ratio. In Royston and Parmar's 2013 simulations, log-rank significance levels remained close to their planned value under the studied proportional and nonproportional patterns, while power differed. That illustrates why a model assumption, a test's calibration and its power are separate questions; it is not proof that every survival analysis is valid."
}
